Releasing version mvm02b.  This one may be too tough, since you
*really* have to watch what you're doing to avoid penalties.

http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/patches.shtml#mvm

I'd really be interested in how you feel this patch affects the Monk's
balance, and whether you think it's too negative.  Also, is the
inventory challenge interesting/fun, or just pathetically annoying?

DETAILS SPOILER:

Void depends on amount of items carried in master inventory, and on a
bunch of properties (some good, some bad).  Void is calculated for all
chars, but only affects monk.  Void affects chances to hit monster.
Void affects armor class throughout the game, and is included in the
displayed AC value.

Monk's *starting* inventory tends to be right at no-modifier or one-
negative.  This means that a normal monk that's gathering gear will
end up with a obvious penalty to AC, and a noticeable penalty in
combat.  The easiest way to keep a monk in the positive void zone is
by carrying a bag and using chests.  It's not to the point where
throwing aside your starting armor helps, but hiding your food does
(which can be a problem for the monk's already-strict diet), and using
(eg, to identify), storing, ignoring, or selling (once you find a
chest) most items.

